cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Tender Evaluation Assistant
message: >-
  If you refer to this work, please cite it using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Nasi
    family-names: Purcell
  - given-names: Chenyu
    family-names: Fang
abstract: >-
  An AI-assisted procurement review pipeline for public tender evaluation. A
  tender's documents are parsed into an addressable node tree, the Completeness
  Check Schedule's items are located and turned into a rule set a person confirms,
  and each bid is checked against that confirmed version by a deterministic engine.
  Every value carries a citation to the page it came from, a reviewer can correct
  any of them with a reason, and the verdict is re-decided without a model call.
keywords:
  - tender evaluation
  - document understanding
  - PDF parsing
  - retrieval
  - large language models
  - human in the loop
repository-code: https://github.com/tender-eval-ai/tender-evaluation-assistant
